{%- comment -%}
  ONE entry of the variant-gallery-embed JSON island, printed as a JSON object,
  or NOTHING when the entry would not be emitted (no usable image URL, a video
  without poster or sources, a model without a GLB source, a URL that is not a
  YouTube/Vimeo link, ...).

  Why a snippet. The island in blocks/variant-gallery-embed.liquid used to carry
  the same object bodies nineteen times (one per call site and path). Copies
  drift, and they cost the extension's 100 KiB Liquid budget every time.

  Parameters (everything optional; what is missing is nil):
    m        a Shopify media or image object (image, video, external video,
             model) -- or nil for the URL and metafield-model modes
    kind     forces the type of `m`; only 'image' is ever passed, for
             variant.featured_image (an image object has no media_type)
    alt      raw alt text (item.alt, media.alt) or nil
    fb       fallback alt text (variant.title or product.title); the object's
             alt is `alt | default: fb`
    url      an external video URL: URL mode (parsed by cp-external-video, the
             ONE Liquid URL parser)
    model    a model URL from custom.variant_3d_models: metafield-model mode
    preview  the preview image URL belonging to `model` (nil when there is none)

  Precedence: url, then model, then kind / m.media_type.

  Strictness: the callers decide WHICH entries reach this snippet. In particular
  the file_reference loops (custom.variant_gallery) hand over only `image` and
  `video` items -- Shopify's list.file_reference never yields external videos or
  models, and the earlier code emitted nothing for them either.

  ESCAPE RULE. The object is collected in `cp_i_out` and printed ONCE with `<`
  and `>` replaced by their JSON escapes. That replaces the per-value replace on
  the alt text (R3-H1: `| json` does not neutralise `<`, so an alt text with
  `</script>` would close the island's <script> element) and has two
  consequences, both wanted:
    1. The output contains NO `<` and NO `>` at all. JSON structure never uses
       them; they can only sit inside string values, where the escape is valid
       JSON that JSON.parse turns back. So the caller's cut of Shopify's
       "<!-- BEGIN app snippet ... -->" annotation provably cannot cut into the
       object, and the island's fallback memo can use `<` and `>` as separators.
    2. model_src and the video src, which were only `| json` before, can no
       longer leave the <script> element either.

  CALLERS MUST CUT SHOPIFY'S ANNOTATION from the captured output, exactly as for
  cp-external-video (see its header; the cut is a no-op on an unannotated
  value). Every call site is these three lines:

    {%- capture cp_o -%}{%- render 'cp-vg-item', m: item, alt: item.alt, fb: variant.title -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign cp_o = cp_o | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip -%}
    {%- if cp_o != blank -%}{%- if cp_has_any %},{% endif -%}{{ cp_o }}{%- assign cp_has_any = true -%}{%- endif -%}

  The comma and `cp_has_any` stay with the caller: `render` is scope-isolated,
  so this snippet knows no state.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture cp_i_out -%}
  {%- assign cp_i_alt = alt | default: fb | json -%}
  {%- assign cp_i_kind = kind | default: m.media_type -%}
  {%- if url != blank -%}
    {%- capture cp_i_pair -%}{%- render 'cp-external-video', url: url -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign cp_i_pair = cp_i_pair | split: '-->' | last | split: '<!--' | first | strip -%}
    {%- assign cp_i_host = cp_i_pair | split: '|' | first | default: '' -%}
    {%- assign cp_i_id = cp_i_pair | split: '|' | last | default: '' -%}
    {%- comment -%} Only what cp-external-video can answer. The host is also interpolated into an embed URL by the controller, so anything else is refused here instead of trusted. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if cp_i_host == 'youtube' or cp_i_host == 'vimeo' -%}
      {%- if cp_i_id != blank -%}
        {%- assign cp_i_thumb = '' -%}
        {%- if cp_i_host == 'youtube' -%}
          {%- assign cp_i_thumb = 'https://img.youtube.com/vi/' | append: cp_i_id | append: '/hqdefault.jpg' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {"type":"external_video","thumb":{{ cp_i_thumb | json }},"poster":{{ cp_i_thumb | json }},"w":0,"h":0,"alt":{{ cp_i_alt }},"host":{{ cp_i_host | json }},"external_id":{{ cp_i_id | json }}}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- elsif model != blank -%}
    {%- assign cp_i_pv = preview | default: '' -%}
    {"type":"model","thumb":{{ cp_i_pv | json }},"poster":{{ cp_i_pv | json }},"w":800,"h":800,"alt":{{ cp_i_alt }},"model_src":{{ model | json }}}
  {%- elsif cp_i_kind == 'image' -%}
    {%- assign cp_i_src = m | image_url: width: 800 -%}
    {%- if cp_i_src != blank -%}
      {%- assign cp_i_w = m.preview_image.width | default: m.width -%}
      {%- assign cp_i_h = m.preview_image.height | default: m.height -%}
      {"type":"image","src_400":{{ m | image_url: width: 400 | json }},"src_800":{{ cp_i_src | json }},"src_1200":{{ m | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},"thumb":{{ m | image_url: width: 160 | json }},"w":{{ cp_i_w | json }},"h":{{ cp_i_h | json }},"alt":{{ cp_i_alt }}}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- elsif m.preview_image != blank -%}
    {%- assign cp_i_pi = m.preview_image -%}
    {%- capture cp_i_media -%}"thumb":{{ cp_i_pi | image_url: width: 160 | json }},"poster":{{ cp_i_pi | image_url: width: 1200 | json }},"w":{{ cp_i_pi.width | json }},"h":{{ cp_i_pi.height | json }},"alt":{{ cp_i_alt }}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if cp_i_kind == 'video' and m.sources.size > 0 -%}
      {"type":"video",{{ cp_i_media }},"sources":[
      {%- for s in m.sources -%}
        {%- unless forloop.first %},{% endunless -%}
        {"src":{{ s.url | json }},"mime":{{ s.mime_type | json }}}
      {%- endfor -%}
      ]}
    {%- elsif cp_i_kind == 'external_video' -%}
      {"type":"external_video",{{ cp_i_media }},"host":{{ m.host | json }},"external_id":{{ m.external_id | json }}}
    {%- elsif cp_i_kind == 'model' -%}
      {%- assign cp_i_glb = blank -%}
      {%- for s in m.sources -%}
        {%- assign cp_i_fmt = s.format | downcase -%}
        {%- if cp_i_fmt == 'glb' and cp_i_glb == blank -%}{%- assign cp_i_glb = s.url -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if cp_i_glb != blank -%}
        {"type":"model",{{ cp_i_media }},"model_src":{{ cp_i_glb | json }}}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{{- cp_i_out | replace: "<", "\u003c" | replace: ">", "\u003e" -}}
